From 2bda83b2d94d9e54958b233ef0f26d118038e74a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 01:05:21 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 012/104] Unified: one integrated working environment instead
 of a choice of workbenches

- New module Unified with the only workbench shown to the user. Its
  toolbars carry the main flow (sketch, pad/pocket/revolution/hole,
  fillet/chamfer/thickness, patterns, parts, measure); the Sketch and
  Part Design menus hold all other tools of Sketcher and PartDesign.
- While a sketch is edited, the Sketcher edit mode toolbars replace the
  modelling toolbars in the same workbench (Sketcher now also hides the
  Unified toolbars and saves the edit mode toolbar state there).
- Single workbench mode (Config "SingleWorkbench", set by FreeCAD's
  main): requests to activate another workbench (start page, editing a
  sketch or a PartDesign feature, the remembered last module, ...)
  activate the integrated one instead; the workbench selector, the
  View > Workbench menu and the Workbenches preference page are gone.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
